       These system calls create and operate on a timer  that  delivers  timer
       expiration notifications via a file descriptor.  They provide an alter‐
       native  to  the use of sseettiittiimmeerr(2) or ttiimmeerr__ccrreeaattee(2), with the advan‐
       tage that the file descriptor may be monitored by  sseelleecctt(2),  ppoollll(2),
       and eeppoollll(7).

       The  use  of  these  three  system  calls  is  analogous  to the use of
       ttiimmeerr__ccrreeaattee(2), ttiimmeerr__sseettttiimmee(2), and ttiimmeerr__ggeettttiimmee(2).  (There is  no
       analog  of ttiimmeerr__ggeettoovveerrrruunn(2), since that functionality is provided by
       rreeaadd(2), as described below.)

