              CCLLOOCCKK__RREEAALLTTIIMMEE is not suitable for such applications, since that
              clock is affected by discontinuous changes to the system clock.

       CCLLOOCCKK__RREEAALLTTIIMMEE__AALLAARRMM (since Linux 3.11)
              This clock is like CCLLOOCCKK__RREEAALLTTIIMMEE, but will wake the  system  if
              it  is suspended.  The caller must have the CCAAPP__WWAAKKEE__AALLAARRMM capa‐
              bility in order to set a timer against this clock.

       CCLLOOCCKK__BBOOOOTTTTIIMMEE__AALLAARRMM (since Linux 3.11)
              This clock is like CCLLOOCCKK__BBOOOOTTTTIIMMEE, but will wake the  system  if
